# Header Notification Bell Rules

## Bell Button Behavior
- The bell button must ALWAYS open the notification dropdown panel when the user is authenticated.
- The bell button must NEVER redirect to /settings or any other page for authenticated users.
- `pushEnabled` / `useNotificationSettings` must NOT be used in Header.tsx — push notification settings only control whether push messages are sent to the device, NOT whether the user can view notifications in the app.

## Notification Fetching
- `fetchNotifications` must only check `status === "authenticated"`, nothing else.
- Do NOT gate notification fetching behind `pushEnabled` or any localStorage flag.

## Summary of Past Bug
- Previously, `pushEnabled` (from localStorage `push_notification_enabled`) was used to gate the bell click, causing it to redirect to `/settings` when the flag was `false` (default for most users). This bug has been fixed multiple times and must not be reintroduced.
